//github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/dde3b70c6e5b8c25d1ed6ed7fdabf2355b93cd93/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:07:32Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:07:32Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"fix: let runtime settings override ones baked in at build\n\ngetEnvVar preferred the build-time value, so a prebuilt image reported\nwhatever was in the .env when it was compiled rather than how it was actually\nstarted. On the published image that meant DL_DB_BACKEND always read as\nsqlite, even with Postgres configured.\n\nThe loader also gated itself on the baked DL_ENV_TYPE, so a build and a run\nthat disagreed never fetched runtime config at all. It now asks the server\nunless the build was for a managed instance, and treats the server''s refusal\nas an ordinary answer rather than an error worth reporting.","tree":{"sha":"7734ba2a07759966d968c884933e014a3361f1cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/7734ba2a07759966d968c884933e014a3361f1cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/dde3b70c6e5b8c25d1ed6ed7fdabf2355b93cd93","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/dde3b70c6e5b8c25d1ed6ed7fdabf2355b93cd93","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKGRkZTNiNzBjNmU1YjhjMjVkMWVkNmVkN2ZkYWJmMjM1NWI5M2NkOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/1bc14432f1c4ade1077949c6fbbb074f4de6b55a","sha":"1bc14432f1c4ade1077949c6fbbb074f4de6b55a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/1bc14432f1c4ade1077949c6fbbb074f4de6b55a"}],"sha":"dde3b70c6e5b8c25d1ed6ed7fdabf2355b93cd93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/dde3b70c6e5b8c25d1ed6ed7fdabf2355b93cd93"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/1bc14432f1c4ade1077949c6fbbb074f4de6b55a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:07:25Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:07:25Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"fix: read the .env file when the built server starts\n\nNitro only loads dotenv in dev, so `node dist/analog/server/index.mjs` saw\nnone of the settings the docs tell people to put in .env. DL_PG_* never\nreached the process, the app quietly fell back to SQLite, and deploying from\nsource had never worked without exporting every variable by hand.\n\nA plugin loads the file on startup. Real environment variables still take\nprecedence, so Docker and hosted platforms are unaffected, and DL_ENV_FILE\npoints it somewhere else. It has to stay synchronous, because Nitro calls\nplugins without awaiting them.","tree":{"sha":"f8c5a7ff7334524580bdcc2403b2d06c94ddd397","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/f8c5a7ff7334524580bdcc2403b2d06c94ddd397"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/1bc14432f1c4ade1077949c6fbbb074f4de6b55a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/1bc14432f1c4ade1077949c6fbbb074f4de6b55a","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKDFiYzE0NDMyZjFjNGFkZTEwNzc5NDljNmZiYmIwNzRmNGRlNmI1NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/03982dd7e60c428e9bbca994823c08137bac895d","sha":"03982dd7e60c428e9bbca994823c08137bac895d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/03982dd7e60c428e9bbca994823c08137bac895d"}],"sha":"1bc14432f1c4ade1077949c6fbbb074f4de6b55a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/1bc14432f1c4ade1077949c6fbbb074f4de6b55a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/03982dd7e60c428e9bbca994823c08137bac895d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:07:18Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:07:18Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"fix: address and authenticate API requests correctly\n\nTwo bugs in how the client picks where to send a request.\n\nIn the browser, baseUrl() used DL_BASE_URL as the API base. That value is\nbaked into the bundle at build time, so anyone who set it to anything other\nthan the exact origin they browse from had every request blocked as\ncross-origin. Setting it to a dev URL and then serving on :3000 was enough to\nbreak the whole app. The API is served by the same app, so a relative URL is\nalways right. DL_BASE_URL goes back to being the sitemap host and an extra\nallowed origin.\n\nDuring server rendering there are no cookies of our own, so every fetch on a\npassword-protected instance came back 401 and failed silently. Pages rendered\nempty and only filled in once the browser took over. The request''s cookie\nheader is now passed through. A request without a session still renders\nnothing, so this doesn''t widen what an unauthenticated visitor can see.","tree":{"sha":"2e9d117270d253ea35593419c8945b28eac8c707","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/2e9d117270d253ea35593419c8945b28eac8c707"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/03982dd7e60c428e9bbca994823c08137bac895d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/03982dd7e60c428e9bbca994823c08137bac895d","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKDAzOTgyZGQ3ZTYwYzQyOGU5YmJjYTk5NDgyM2MwODEzN2JhYzg5NWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/cd5222801d8a1a3cf8a9bf2dd75fe473b660b8ad","sha":"cd5222801d8a1a3cf8a9bf2dd75fe473b660b8ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/cd5222801d8a1a3cf8a9bf2dd75fe473b660b8ad"}],"sha":"03982dd7e60c428e9bbca994823c08137bac895d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/03982dd7e60c428e9bbca994823c08137bac895d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/cd5222801d8a1a3cf8a9bf2dd75fe473b660b8ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:07:00Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:07:00Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"fix: keep domain fields a partial edit did not carry\n\nupdateDomain wrote expiry_date, registration_date, updated_date and notes as\n`value ?? null`, so an edit that omitted one cleared it. A notes-only PUT\nwiped the expiry date.\n\nOnly columns present in the input are written now. The edit form always sends\nevery field, so the UI was safe, but the API accepts partial bodies and\nquietly destroyed data for anyone using it directly.","tree":{"sha":"ab67123965a8727e4a4a74defc2f68ee38b9b317","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/ab67123965a8727e4a4a74defc2f68ee38b9b317"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/cd5222801d8a1a3cf8a9bf2dd75fe473b660b8ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/cd5222801d8a1a3cf8a9bf2dd75fe473b660b8ad","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKGNkNTIyMjgwMWQ4YTFhM2NmOGE5YmYyZGQ3NWZlNDczYjY2MGI4YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/919a85b50f58fc12f02790afebdeb480934ed359","sha":"919a85b50f58fc12f02790afebdeb480934ed359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/919a85b50f58fc12f02790afebdeb480934ed359"}],"sha":"cd5222801d8a1a3cf8a9bf2dd75fe473b660b8ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/cd5222801d8a1a3cf8a9bf2dd75fe473b660b8ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/919a85b50f58fc12f02790afebdeb480934ed359/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:06:53Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:06:53Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"fix: clear the domain cache when a query group writes\n\nThe cache added in 960bdc3 only watched saveDomain, updateDomain and\ndeleteDomain. The domain list carries its relations, so editing a tag, link,\ncosting or subdomain left every page showing stale data until a full reload.\n\nMatching on the verb covers each query group without a list to keep in step\nwith the services, and the proxy now wraps the groups themselves.\n\nInvalidation also moved from call time to completion. Clearing before the\nwrite landed left a window where an overlapping read could put the pre-write\nrows straight back into the cache.","tree":{"sha":"dfb998369a2737e66905faf4b8b7c29dc625a3b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/dfb998369a2737e66905faf4b8b7c29dc625a3b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/919a85b50f58fc12f02790afebdeb480934ed359","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/919a85b50f58fc12f02790afebdeb480934ed359","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKDkxOWE4NWI1MGY1OGZjMTJmMDI3OTBhZmViZGViNDgwOTM0ZWQzNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/c0f80321272f550d3873e8efe0a7d8eb9cc95505","sha":"c0f80321272f550d3873e8efe0a7d8eb9cc95505","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/c0f80321272f550d3873e8efe0a7d8eb9cc95505"}],"sha":"919a85b50f58fc12f02790afebdeb480934ed359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/919a85b50f58fc12f02790afebdeb480934ed359"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/c0f80321272f550d3873e8efe0a7d8eb9cc95505/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:26:27Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:26:27Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"fix: save the host returned by the domain lookup\n\nlinkHost read host[''ip''] and host[''as_number''], but the lookup API returns\nip-api''s field names: query, as and regionName. The guard on host[''ip''] was\ntherefore never true, and no host was written on either create or update. The\nupdater job already maps those names, so a host only appeared after the next\nscheduled refresh.\n\nhostColumns() accepts either spelling, matching what the Supabase service and\nthe updater job already do.\n\nThe existing test passed a host whose fields were already mapped to column\nnames, which is why it never caught this. The new one uses the shape the\nlookup actually returns.","tree":{"sha":"97611f51bd6e28319b43773cad144c1344b93401","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/97611f51bd6e28319b43773cad144c1344b93401"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/c0f80321272f550d3873e8efe0a7d8eb9cc95505","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/c0f80321272f550d3873e8efe0a7d8eb9cc95505","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKGMwZjgwMzIxMjcyZjU1MGQzODczZThlZmUwYTdkOGViOWNjOTU1MDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/c7c43d93cd2276fd56584ef140e761fd5f729223","sha":"c7c43d93cd2276fd56584ef140e761fd5f729223","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/c7c43d93cd2276fd56584ef140e761fd5f729223"}],"sha":"c0f80321272f550d3873e8efe0a7d8eb9cc95505","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/c0f80321272f550d3873e8efe0a7d8eb9cc95505"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/c7c43d93cd2276fd56584ef140e761fd5f729223/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:26:17Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:26:17Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"fix: subscribe to saveDomain, so adding a domain sends a request\n\nonSubmit awaited the observable that saveDomain returns. Awaiting a\nnon-thenable resolves straight away, nothing subscribed, and HttpClient sends\nnothing until it has a subscriber. The page then showed a success toast and\nnavigated, so the domain looked saved and never was. The full form and\nquick-add were both affected.\n\nIt worked before the data layer moved onto HttpClient, because supabase-js\nbuilders and the old fetch-based pg util each run without a subscriber.\n\n@typescript-eslint/await-thenable now catches the pattern. It needs type-aware\nlinting, which takes lint to about 6s, and it found three more cases:\n\n- deleteSubdomainsByDomain awaited fetchDomainId and passed the observable\n  itself as a query filter, so it could never have deleted anything. Nothing\n  calls it, so no behaviour changes\n- deleteAccount awaited getToken, which returns a string\n- The bulk notification page awaited a Subscription","tree":{"sha":"36442802e012f22906746bbad695cf5a8f5fdf00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/36442802e012f22906746bbad695cf5a8f5fdf00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/c7c43d93cd2276fd56584ef140e761fd5f729223","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/c7c43d93cd2276fd56584ef140e761fd5f729223","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKGM3YzQzZDkzY2QyMjc2ZmQ1NjU4NGVmMTQwZTc2MWZkNWY3MjkyMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/9164041a54f8f475a119036461898f63f922de07","sha":"9164041a54f8f475a119036461898f63f922de07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/9164041a54f8f475a119036461898f63f922de07"}],"sha":"c7c43d93cd2276fd56584ef140e761fd5f729223","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/c7c43d93cd2276fd56584ef140e761fd5f729223"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/9164041a54f8f475a119036461898f63f922de07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:26:09Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:26:09Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"fix: reject malformed ids instead of passing them to the driver\n\nA request for /v1/domains/not-a-uuid reached Postgres as a uuid comparison\nand came back as a 500 carrying an unhandled driver error, while SQLite\ncompared it as text and answered 404. Route params were never validated.\n\nuuidParam() checks the shape before the query runs, so both backends now\nanswer 400. Only hand-written requests can trigger it, since the client\nbuilds its URLs from ids the server issued, but it was a 500 on user input\nand a difference in behaviour between the two backends.","tree":{"sha":"8f1c2848fdd1d9034534b178ad75b28600df4794","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/8f1c2848fdd1d9034534b178ad75b28600df4794"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/9164041a54f8f475a119036461898f63f922de07","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/9164041a54f8f475a119036461898f63f922de07","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKDkxNjQwNDFhNTRmOGY0NzVhMTE5MDM2NDYxODk4ZjYzZjkyMmRlMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/1beb1e0528ed87e6907f27edbe3e9c01353e45a3","sha":"1beb1e0528ed87e6907f27edbe3e9c01353e45a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/1beb1e0528ed87e6907f27edbe3e9c01353e45a3"}],"sha":"9164041a54f8f475a119036461898f63f922de07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/9164041a54f8f475a119036461898f63f922de07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/1beb1e0528ed87e6907f27edbe3e9c01353e45a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:26:01Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:26:01Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"fix: serve the /v1 API on the dev server\n\nAnalog''s dev server only forwards /api requests to Nitro, so every /v1 call\nfell through to the app and came back as the 404 page. Reads, writes and\neverything else in self-hosted mode were unusable under npm run dev.\nProduction is a plain Nitro server and was never affected, which is why the\nexisting specs, which all boot the built server, missed it.\n\nA serve-only Vite plugin re-prefixes /v1 so Analog forwards it, and Nitro\nstrips the prefix again. Nitro therefore sees the same URL it serves directly\nin production. Routing through /api permanently is not an option, because\nAnalog''s API middleware $fetches GET requests and loses the status code and\nbody of any error.\n\nThe new spec boots the dev server and checks reads, writes and error\nenvelopes. Its helper clears VITEST from the child environment, since Analog\nskips creating the Nitro dev server when it detects a test run.","tree":{"sha":"4fa1e0ff0312a7039d66d79b67351c1fe1ef6198","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/4fa1e0ff0312a7039d66d79b67351c1fe1ef6198"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/1beb1e0528ed87e6907f27edbe3e9c01353e45a3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/1beb1e0528ed87e6907f27edbe3e9c01353e45a3","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKDFiZWIxZTA1MjhlZDg3ZTY5MDdmMjdlZGJlM2U5YzAxMzUzZTQ1YTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/ae45b03f77373af020e7d9846de24f32ca49ca60","sha":"ae45b03f77373af020e7d9846de24f32ca49ca60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/ae45b03f77373af020e7d9846de24f32ca49ca60"}],"sha":"1beb1e0528ed87e6907f27edbe3e9c01353e45a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/1beb1e0528ed87e6907f27edbe3e9c01353e45a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/ae45b03f77373af020e7d9846de24f32ca49ca60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T17:00:52Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T17:00:52Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"fix: refuse the self-hosted API and migrations on managed instances\n\nThe /v1 routes and the migration runner shipped in the same bundle as the\nmanaged build, so hitting /v1/domains on a managed instance would have stood\nup its own SQLite database and served from it, outside Supabase and its RLS.\n\nBoth now refuse when DL_ENV_TYPE is managed, covered by tests that boot the\nbuilt server in managed mode and assert reads, writes and job triggers are\nall rejected.","tree":{"sha":"4fe4c434705667da441b29cd22d130dda861fecf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/4fe4c434705667da441b29cd22d130dda861fecf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/ae45b03f77373af020e7d9846de24f32ca49ca60","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/ae45b03f77373af020e7d9846de24f32ca49ca60","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKGFlNDViMDNmNzczNzNhZjAyMGU3ZDk4NDZkZTI0ZjMyY2E0OWNhNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/960bdc3b8c114a4e3c4ee5eca61f634de488c63c","sha":"960bdc3b8c114a4e3c4ee5eca61f634de488c63c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/960bdc3b8c114a4e3c4ee5eca61f634de488c63c"}],"sha":"ae45b03f77373af020e7d9846de24f32ca49ca60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/ae45b03f77373af020e7d9846de24f32ca49ca60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/960bdc3b8c114a4e3c4ee5eca61f634de488c63c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:57:58Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:57:58Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"perf: cache the domain list, batch uptime, and stop leaking subscriptions\n\nPhase 5, partial. The changes here are the ones that can be verified without\na browser; see below for what is deliberately left.\n\n- The domain list is fetched once and shared, rather than re-fetched by each\n  of the nine pages that needed it. Writes through the service drop the cache,\n  so an edit still shows up immediately\n- The monitor page asked for uptime history one domain at a time. It now makes\n  a single request via /v1/uptime/history, falling back to the per-domain calls\n  on the Supabase path, which is left untouched\n- Route params, router events and form valueChanges were subscribed without\n  teardown in eleven pages, so navigating away left handlers running. They now\n  use takeUntilDestroyed. The remaining subscriptions are one-shot HTTP calls,\n  which complete on their own\n- The tag cloud imported all of d3 to use a single function; it now imports\n  d3-selection, and d3 is no longer a dependency\n\nNot done here, and why:\n- Replacing the 65-module PrimeNG barrel is the largest bundle win available\n  (the main chunk is 2.3 MB), but it touches all 133 components that import it,\n  and gives nothing until every one is converted. Worth doing as its own change\n- OnPush on the chart and list components needs interactive verification to be\n  sure nothing goes stale, which is not possible here\n- Splitting the 836-line SupabaseService is managed-path work, and is better\n  done alongside the Phase 6 decision than before it\n\nNote @angular/cdk looked unused but is required by PrimeNG''s picklist, which\nthe tag editor uses. Removing it broke the build, so it stays.","tree":{"sha":"4287f3da460bf5d78e30782307a8e6ab2c26017b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/4287f3da460bf5d78e30782307a8e6ab2c26017b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/960bdc3b8c114a4e3c4ee5eca61f634de488c63c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/960bdc3b8c114a4e3c4ee5eca61f634de488c63c","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKDk2MGJkYzNiOGMxMTRhNGUzYzRlZTVlY2E2MWY2MzRkZTQ4OGM2M2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/d6a7d94404419b0592ed0f5df5234deb958ef267","sha":"d6a7d94404419b0592ed0f5df5234deb958ef267","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/d6a7d94404419b0592ed0f5df5234deb958ef267"}],"sha":"960bdc3b8c114a4e3c4ee5eca61f634de488c63c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/960bdc3b8c114a4e3c4ee5eca61f634de488c63c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/d6a7d94404419b0592ed0f5df5234deb958ef267/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:48:28Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:48:28Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"feat: make SQLite the default for new installs, in one container\n\nPhase 4. A fresh install is now one container and one volume, with no\ndatabase to configure. Existing installs are untouched.\n\n- docker-compose.yml is a single service with a data volume. The previous\n  app + postgres + updater file is kept verbatim as\n  docker-compose.postgres.yml, and still works as it always did\n- The image declares /data and defaults DL_SQLITE_PATH into it\n- start.sh only waits for Postgres when Postgres is configured, so the\n  container no longer exits when DL_PG_* is absent\n- install.sh no longer overwrites an existing docker-compose.yml\n\nBackend choice is unchanged for anyone already running: DL_PG_* present means\nPostgres, exactly as before. Verified by upgrading a 0.2.4 Postgres database\nin place, which is baselined rather than replayed, keeps its rows, and only\npicks up the new migration.\n\nFor anyone who wants to consolidate, npm run migrate:pg-to-sqlite copies a\nPostgres database into a SQLite file, reading only from the source, and can be\nre-run safely.\n\nAlso:\n- The Helm updater CronJob is off by default, since the app schedules its own\n  jobs. Enabling it now triggers each job once and exits; previously it ran\n  crond in the foreground, so every daily run left another pod running forever\n- Triggering a job route externally logs a one-off note pointing at the\n  upgrade guide, rather than silently duplicating the scheduler''s work\n- New self-hosting/upgrading guide covering what happens automatically, what\n  can be removed, and how to move to SQLite\n- CI now smoke-tests the zero-config SQLite install alongside the Postgres one","tree":{"sha":"b9859486be1aec6a2a61b264f991be6e50c5ac8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/b9859486be1aec6a2a61b264f991be6e50c5ac8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/d6a7d94404419b0592ed0f5df5234deb958ef267","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/d6a7d94404419b0592ed0f5df5234deb958ef267","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKGQ2YTdkOTQ0MDQ0MTliMDU5MmVkMGY1ZGY1MjM0ZGViOTU4ZWYyNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/85a16fd4bb9503dfc1080a3eeeefcfd447011efb","sha":"85a16fd4bb9503dfc1080a3eeeefcfd447011efb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/85a16fd4bb9503dfc1080a3eeeefcfd447011efb"}],"sha":"d6a7d94404419b0592ed0f5df5234deb958ef267","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/d6a7d94404419b0592ed0f5df5234deb958ef267"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/85a16fd4bb9503dfc1080a3eeeefcfd447011efb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:37:42Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:37:42Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"feat: run scheduled jobs from inside the app, under database locks\n\nPhase 3. Self-hosted instances no longer need the companion cron container,\nand the jobs work on either database.\n\nScheduling\n- The app schedules its own jobs (monitor, updater, reminders, cleanup) with\n  per-job intervals set by env var, or DL_DISABLE_SCHEDULER to opt out\n- Every job runs under a database lock recorded in a new job_runs table, so a\n  legacy updater container curling the old routes cannot duplicate work that\n  the internal scheduler is already doing. A lock left by a crashed run is\n  taken over after thirty minutes\n- The four legacy routes remain as manual triggers, now thin wrappers around\n  the same locked runner, and accept DL_API_KEY so a scheduler can call in\n\nJobs\n- Monitor, reminders and cleanup now go through the repositories, so they work\n  on SQLite as well as Postgres\n- Uptime checks time DNS, the TLS handshake and the request separately, so the\n  columns that were always null now carry real numbers\n- Reminders match a window rather than an exact day count, so a missed run no\n  longer loses the reminder entirely\n- The updater takes least-recently-updated domains first, in capped batches,\n  and retries with backoff, which is what the WHOIS rate-limit reports needed\n- One notification path for every job: record, then fan out to the configured\n  channels\n\nWHOIS now tries RDAP first, falling back through the other sources. RDAP is\nstructured and resolves its endpoint per TLD from the IANA bootstrap, so it\navoids most of the rate limiting and parse failures of port-43 WHOIS. The\norder is overridable with DL_WHOIS_PROVIDERS.\n\nThe updater''s internals moved from src/server/routes to src/server/jobs. They\nwere being scanned as HTTP routes purely because of where they sat, and had\nnever been type-checked; doing so surfaced a crash in the registrar update\nwhen a lookup returned no registrar.","tree":{"sha":"3759f9259663a5d9097b4b6fc8547d9b23bc9995","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/3759f9259663a5d9097b4b6fc8547d9b23bc9995"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/85a16fd4bb9503dfc1080a3eeeefcfd447011efb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/85a16fd4bb9503dfc1080a3eeeefcfd447011efb","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKDg1YTE2ZmQ0YmI5NTAzZGZjMTA4MGEzZWVlZWZjZmQ0NDcwMTFlZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/ec0d36b8deceaf966482c7efbea2d2441d7757f3","sha":"ec0d36b8deceaf966482c7efbea2d2441d7757f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/ec0d36b8deceaf966482c7efbea2d2441d7757f3"}],"sha":"85a16fd4bb9503dfc1080a3eeeefcfd447011efb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/85a16fd4bb9503dfc1080a3eeeefcfd447011efb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/ec0d36b8deceaf966482c7efbea2d2441d7757f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:26:44Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:26:44Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"refactor: move self-hosted data access onto the API, delete the pg client tree\n\nPhase 2. Self-hosted instances now read and write through /v1 instead of\nsending SQL from the browser. Managed still runs the Supabase path.\n\n- New ApiDatabaseService plus per-area query classes, matching the Supabase\n  services method for method so calling code is unchanged. Roughly a tenth of\n  the size of the tree it replaces\n- Deleted db-query-services/pg (14 files), pg-database.service.ts,\n  pg-api.util.ts and pg-executer.ts itself. Net 2,600 fewer lines\n- The browser no longer holds database credentials. The advanced \"database\n  connection\" page is now a read-only status view that offers to clear\n  credentials older versions left in local storage\n- Backend selection moved server-side: the client is told which database is\n  in use (DL_DB_BACKEND), never how to reach it\n\nThe four scheduled jobs call the database in process rather than posting SQL\nto the app over loopback HTTP, which is what made them fragile behind proxies\nand in containers (#101, #102). Their SQL is now dialect-portable except the\nuptime aggregation, which needs data-modifying CTEs and stays Postgres-only\nuntil Phase 3 moves the jobs onto the repositories.\n\nFixes carried with the swap:\n- getDomainUptime returned a raw PostgREST envelope on Supabase and a plain\n  array on Postgres, so three call sites carried shape-guessing hacks. It now\n  returns UptimeRow[] on both, and the hacks are gone\n- The UptimeData interface existed in four copies; it is now declared once\n- sd_info is returned as the JSON string the UI parses, on both dialects\n\nAlso fixes a deadlock the dual-dialect tests caught: a repository queried the\nouter connection inside a transaction, which blocks forever on SQLite''s single\nconnection. Every nested query now takes the transaction.","tree":{"sha":"92f366291b30c7e7148c7a0a95c7ee7bc7b3be75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/92f366291b30c7e7148c7a0a95c7ee7bc7b3be75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/ec0d36b8deceaf966482c7efbea2d2441d7757f3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/ec0d36b8deceaf966482c7efbea2d2441d7757f3","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKGVjMGQzNmI4ZGVjZWFmOTY2NDgyYzdlZmJlYTJkMjQ0MWQ3NzU3ZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/0e729d0f79cb56ba4d26e3c1af9515b4e5b7fa02","sha":"0e729d0f79cb56ba4d26e3c1af9515b4e5b7fa02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/0e729d0f79cb56ba4d26e3c1af9515b4e5b7fa02"}],"sha":"ec0d36b8deceaf966482c7efbea2d2441d7757f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/ec0d36b8deceaf966482c7efbea2d2441d7757f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/0e729d0f79cb56ba4d26e3c1af9515b4e5b7fa02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:25:29Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:25:29Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"feat: add the server-side data core behind a typed /v1 API\n\nPhase 1 of the data-layer overhaul. Nothing in the client uses this yet, so\nbehaviour is unchanged; the point is to have one place where data access\nlives, working against both Postgres and SQLite.\n\nData core\n- One Kysely `Database` type matching the existing 21 tables exactly, so\n  established Postgres installs need no schema changes at all\n- Backend picked from the environment: DL_PG_* present keeps Postgres,\n  otherwise SQLite at DL_SQLITE_PATH. A fresh install now needs no database\n  configuration whatsoever\n- Migration runner with baseline detection: an existing database is recorded\n  as already migrated rather than having DDL replayed over live tables.\n  Migrations are versioned, additive and transactional, and run once on first\n  use rather than at build time\n- Postgres type parsers are scoped to this pool, so the legacy pg-executer\n  path keeps its current behaviour\n\nRepositories\n- src/server/db/repos/ covers domains, tags, notifications, links, assets,\n  history, uptime and admin, replacing the Postgres-only LATERAL/jsonb query\n  with batched fetches that behave identically on both dialects\n- Every query is scoped to the owning user, and deletes verify ownership\n  first, so the repo layer is safe to expose to a multi-user front end later\n- Fixes carried over from the audit: tags can be renamed (the old UPDATE\n  matched on the column it was setting), addTag no longer drops user_id, and\n  changes are attributed to the domain''s real owner\n\nAPI\n- /v1 endpoints with zod-validated input and one error envelope carrying a\n  stable code, a safe message and the offending field. Driver errors never\n  reach the caller. Mounted at /v1 rather than /api/v1 because Analog''s\n  /api proxy re-fetches GETs and would discard the status and body\n- Optional authentication: set DL_AUTH_PASSWORD to require a signed session\n  cookie, DL_API_KEY to let a scheduler call in. Both off by default, so\n  existing instances are unaffected\n- Read-only mode is now enforced on the server, not only in the UI\n\nTesting\n- One contract suite runs against Postgres and SQLite, asserting identical\n  behaviour: 166 server tests covering repositories, migrations, dialect\n  parity and the schema\n- A parity suite fails if the two dialects ever drift on tables, columns or\n  unique constraints\n- API tests exercise the built server over HTTP on a throwaway database,\n  including auth, read-only mode and error shapes; wired into CI after build\n- src/server was never type-checked; tsconfig.server.json now covers the data\n  core, the API and the tests, and `npm run typecheck` runs both projects\n\nAlso adds the toolchain the SQLite driver needs to build on alpine.","tree":{"sha":"4c74eb1072024154c7b9461e6b74f87e937322e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/4c74eb1072024154c7b9461e6b74f87e937322e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/0e729d0f79cb56ba4d26e3c1af9515b4e5b7fa02","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/0e729d0f79cb56ba4d26e3c1af9515b4e5b7fa02","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKDBlNzI5ZDBmNzljYjU2YmE0ZDI2ZTNjMWFmOTUxNWI0ZTViN2ZhMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/3258f658a45628d256d27ce72c7489313f952746","sha":"3258f658a45628d256d27ce72c7489313f952746","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/3258f658a45628d256d27ce72c7489313f952746"}],"sha":"0e729d0f79cb56ba4d26e3c1af9515b4e5b7fa02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/0e729d0f79cb56ba4d26e3c1af9515b4e5b7fa02"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/commits/3258f658a45628d256d27ce72c7489313f952746/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T14:44:29Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T14:44:29Z","email":"alicia@omg.lol","name":"Alicia Sykes"},"message":"fix: close self-hosted credential and cross-origin holes, repair delete_domain\n\nPhase 0 of the data-layer overhaul: a server-side test suite, plus the\nsecurity and correctness fixes that stand on their own.\n\nTest scaffolding\n- Node-environment vitest project under test/, run with `npm run test:server`\n- Schema contract suite covering delete_domain, constraints and idempotency\n- Upgrade suite proving an existing database heals when start.sh re-applies\n  the schema, without losing rows\n- Both wired into CI against a Postgres service container\n\nSecurity\n- /api/env-var returned every DL_/SUPABASE_ variable (including\n  DL_PG_PASSWORD) to unauthenticated callers, and ?key= read any variable\n  at all. Now an explicit client-safe allowlist, with Postgres signalled by\n  a derived DL_PG_ENABLED flag instead of the credentials\n- Vite inlined the same variables into the browser bundle via dynamic\n  import.meta.env access. Client code now reads a build-time allowlist, so\n  secrets cannot reach a chunk\n- /api/pg-executer accepted database credentials from the browser and fell\n  back to server values per-field, letting a caller point the server at\n  their own host and harvest the real password. Credentials are now\n  server-side only, behind DL_ALLOW_CLIENT_DB_CREDENTIALS for anyone still\n  configuring the database from the UI\n- It also reflected any Origin with Allow-Credentials, so any page the user\n  visited could run SQL against their instance. Replaced with a same-origin\n  guard that still admits internal job calls, which send no Origin\n- Raw driver errors are no longer echoed to the caller, and queries run on\n  a pooled connection with a statement timeout\n\nCorrectness\n- delete_domain raised \"column reference domain_id is ambiguous\" on every\n  call, so deleting a domain through the function has never worked. Columns\n  are now qualified, orphan cleanup uses NOT EXISTS and is scoped to the\n  owner, and every child table is covered\n- Deduplicated the second delete_domain, domain_costings and users\n  declarations that shadowed the first\n- domain_updates recorded a hardcoded user id, mis-attributing every change\n  on multi-user instances; it now resolves the domain''s real owner\n- internal-status-info read a header name Node lowercases, so the auth\n  header was always undefined\n- expiration-reminders called .json() on an error Response, throwing while\n  handling a failure; errors now surface properly and console calls are\n  routed through the logger\n- Escaped user input in the contact email, and stripped CR/LF from header\n  values\n- Capped the logger''s in-memory buffer, which grew unbounded","tree":{"sha":"8ce56c66e9a41246a289154aec397d7f8dcaeedc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/trees/8ce56c66e9a41246a289154aec397d7f8dcaeedc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lissy93/domain-locker/git/commits/3258f658a45628d256d27ce72c7489313f952746","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1862727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93","id":1862727,"login":"lissy93","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjI3Mjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lissy93","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lissy93/domain-locker/commit/3258f658a45628d256d27ce72c7489313f952746","node_id":"C_kwDOM79IJNoAKDMy